-// MARK: - In-game HUD editor (0137)
-//
-// A compact panel presented OVER the running game (GameMenu -> "HUD 设置"),
-// not the launcher's full editor: no preview photo, no drag -- the live game
-// is the preview. Every change saves to UserDefaults AND pushes the env var
-// at once (applyOneToEnvironment), so the host applies it on the next
-// present and the HUD in the game moves/resizes/hides in real time.
-// Position is adjusted with X/Y steppers (layout points, +/-10 per tap);
-// size with a 60%-180% slider, like the launcher editor and the button
-// settings. Hide is a TRUE hide (flags bit 0, hud_runtime.c), not off-screen.
-// 0144: the in-game HUD editor, rebuilt as a drag editor like the pad
-// ("按键设置") settings: the five elements are drawn on a preview of the
-// device's own shape, tap one to select it, drag it to move it, a slider for
-// the selected element's own size, and an eye toggle per element to show or
-// hide it. Every change is applied live to the running game (update() calls
-// settings.set + applyOneToEnvironment), so the HUD moves behind the sheet
-// as you drag. The old list + X/Y steppers are gone (the user 2026-11-15
